                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e68773e4-c101-395b-869c-bc1e38d324f3",
                                        "entry_id": "3a482d3b-6650-3981-90f1-58b278392396",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any plant of the genus Anchusa (within family Boraginaceae) of rough and hairy Old World herbs with one-sided clusters of trumpet-shaped flowers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d622893b-e786-4af2-99c5-41be0de013ee",
                                                "sense_id": "e68773e4-c101-395b-869c-bc1e38d324f3",
                                                "text": "1835, Philip Miller, \"Anchusa\", entry in The Gardener's Dictionary, Volume I, 9th Edition, page 430,\nAnchusa and Cinnabar were used by the antients to give an agreeable colour to their ointments; and Pliny tells us that where the anchusa was used, they added salt to prevent the oil in those compositions from becoming rancid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1cf3b05-eda4-464a-8777-89eb18b8ced3",
                                                "sense_id": "e68773e4-c101-395b-869c-bc1e38d324f3",
                                                "text": "Unfortunately, anchusas have the defect of being coarse in appearance, with hairy leaves and stems which are neither elegant nor graceful."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "175f4f90-ce30-465f-a036-03379eacc2d8",
                                                "sense_id": "e68773e4-c101-395b-869c-bc1e38d324f3",
                                                "text": "Related to the common annual form of forget-me-nots (Myosotis), the two species of anchusa produce some of the bluest of the blue flowers in the plant kingdom, and both are easy to grow."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
